NAME
       nl - number lines

SYNOPSIS
       nl [-p] [-b TYPE] [-h TYPE] [-f TYPE] [-v START] [-i
          INCR] [-l N] [-n ln|rn|rz] [-s SEP] [-w WIDTH] [-d
          CC] [file...]

DESCRIPTION
       Number lines. TYPE: a all, t non-empty (default for the
       body), n none, pREGEX lines matching a basic regular
       expression. Lines made only of the delimiter (\: by
       default) three, two or one times start a header, body
       or footer section; a header restarts the numbering
       unless -p.

SEE ALSO
       sh(1)

